  "_tone": "How a line reads, as one word \u2014 the four colours the Budget screen paints. The owner, 2026-09-15: \"any column that needs more money is yellow, negative is red, positive is green\", and Snooze \"turns the column gray\". The ORDER of the tests is the rule: snoozed beats everything (a snoozed line is not asking), over beats short (money already spent that you do not have is worse than money not yet assigned), and short applies only when a target was actually set \u2014 0 means no target, and painting every line without one yellow would make the colour mean nothing. Rows are [budget, needs, snoozed, spent, tone]. The [-5000, 0, false, 6000] row is the one that reaches the \"a target was set\" guard: money moved off the line, a refund landed, available is positive and no target exists. Without the guard `budget < needs` is -5000 < 0 and the line reads as short of nothing. Added 2026-09-15 after a mutation that removed the guard passed every other row.",
