  "_reconcile": "The adjustment a reconcile writes: what the account SHOULD hold minus what the ledger says it does. The sign needs no special case \u2014 a real balance higher than the ledger is money the ledger has not heard about. Zero means no transaction is made at all, because a reconcile that agrees has nothing to record and a 0.00 row would mark the register every time someone checked. Rows are [ledger total, stated total, adjustment].",
